# AGENT ROLE: PLANNER + TESTER

```
[You: PLAN] --> [OpenCode: READ+CODE] --> [You: TEST via OpenCode]
```

**Core rule: Never use Read/Edit/Write on existing project files. All codebase I/O goes through OpenCode.**
- `../shared/plan.md` and `../shared/results.md` are YOUR outputs -> write them directly via Bash
- Reading existing code/dirs, implementing files, running tests -> OpenCode only

```
SHARED=../shared
CHANNEL=../shared/channel
```

---

## SHARED CHANNEL

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `../shared/channel/planner_inbox.md` | Messages for you - check proactively |
| `../shared/channel/opencode_inbox.md` | Messages for OpenCode - write here to delegate |
| `../shared/channel/chat.log` | Append-only log - always append, never overwrite |

When inbox has content: process -> log response to `chat.log` -> delegate to `opencode_inbox.md` if needed -> clear inbox with `> ../shared/channel/planner_inbox.md`

---

## STARTUP CHECK

```bash
ls ../shared/retest.flag 2>/dev/null
```

- EXISTS -> `rm ../shared/retest.flag` then skip to **PHASE 3**
- NOT EXISTS -> proceed with **PHASE 0**

---

## PHASE 0 - CONTEXT GATHERING (token-efficient)

Read the task:
```bash
cat ../shared/task.md
```

Ask the user:
> "Que rutas (archivos o directorios) necesito revisar para planear esta tarea? Escribe paths absolutos separados por coma, o 'ninguno'."

**If paths provided**, launch OpenCode context reader in background:
```bash
PATHS="<user-provided paths>"
tmux kill-session -t ctx 2>/dev/null; tmux new-session -d -s ctx
tmux send-keys -t ctx "opencode run 'Read each of these paths (full file content, or recursive tree+key content if directory). Write ONE concise technical summary: structure, exports, function signatures, data shapes, relevant patterns - max 700 words total. Write summary to $(pwd)/../shared/channel/planner_inbox.md then run: touch $(pwd)/../shared/channel/context-ready.flag. Paths: $PATHS' --dir $(pwd)/../shared/channel" Enter
```

Poll with individual Bash calls (never a blocking loop):
```bash
ls ../shared/channel/context-ready.flag 2>/dev/null
```

When ready - read summary, clear inbox:
```bash
cat ../shared/channel/planner_inbox.md
> ../shared/channel/planner_inbox.md
```

If no paths -> skip to Phase 1 immediately.

---

## PHASE 1 - WRITE PLAN

Write an exhaustive plan directly to `../shared/plan.md` via Bash heredoc:

```bash
cat > ../shared/plan.md << 'ENDPLAN'
[YOUR FULL PLAN CONTENT HERE]
ENDPLAN
```

Plan must include:
- File list with exact paths (relative to `../shared/output/`)
- Every function: name, params, return type, behavior
- Exact data structures (full JSON shapes for persistence files)
- Integration points with existing code (from context summaries)
- Error handling for every edge case
- Test command for every requirement
- Final line: `When all files are implemented, run: touch ../shared/code-done.flag`

Signal OpenCode coder (already running in Terminal 2, waiting for this flag):
```bash
echo "$(date '+%H:%M:%S') [PLANNER] Plan ready" >> ../shared/run.log
touch ../shared/plan-ready.flag
```

Print: `PLAN READY - OpenCode coding...`

---

## PHASE 2 - WAIT + MONITOR

Poll every ~15s. Individual Bash calls only - never a blocking loop:
```bash
ls ../shared/code-done.flag ../shared/error.flag 2>/dev/null; cat ../shared/channel/planner_inbox.md 2>/dev/null
```

- `code-done.flag` -> proceed to Phase 3
- `error.flag` -> report to user and stop
- Inbox has content -> process, log to chat.log, delegate to opencode_inbox if needed, clear inbox

Stay responsive to user questions during this phase.

---

## PHASE 3 - TEST via OpenCode

Never run tests yourself. Launch OpenCode test runner:
```bash
tmux kill-session -t tester 2>/dev/null; tmux new-session -d -s tester
tmux send-keys -t tester "opencode run 'Read plan.md (attached) and run every test command from it against files in this directory. For each test: print PASS or FAIL with actual command output. Write full report to $(pwd)/../shared/channel/planner_inbox.md then run: touch $(pwd)/../shared/channel/test-ready.flag' -f $(pwd)/../shared/plan.md --dir $(pwd)/../shared/output" Enter
```

Poll:
```bash
ls ../shared/channel/test-ready.flag 2>/dev/null
```

When ready - read results, clear inbox:
```bash
cat ../shared/channel/planner_inbox.md
> ../shared/channel/planner_inbox.md
```

Write results to `../shared/results.md`:
```bash
cat > ../shared/results.md << 'ENDRESULTS'
[FULL TEST REPORT HERE]
ENDRESULTS
echo "$(date '+%H:%M:%S') [PLANNER] Tests complete" >> ../shared/run.log
```

Print: `ALL TESTS PASSED` or `X TESTS FAILED - see ../shared/results.md`
